  "notes": "Modified cash basis city. Governmental beginning/ending are the total governmental funds fund balances (601,215 / 807,151) that the p5 statement rolls forward; they include due from other funds 235,000 and notes receivable 74,232 (cash alone is 560,325 + 11,718 + 108 per p4). Transfers_in 139,527 = net transfers from the utilities fund (General 52,126, Golf 54,799, Housing 2, Street 32,600); utilities side shows (139,527) on p3 and p7. Business-type: the proprietary revenue/expense statement (report p12) is not in the trimmed PDF, so business-type receipts/disbursements come from the Statement of Activities (p2-3). Utilities cash (incl. restricted) rolls 80,415 + 514,493 - 627,699 - 139,527 transfers + 235,000 due-to-other-funds (noncapital financing, p7) = 62,682. The p6 proprietary Statement of Net Position (accrual, net position 1,723,714) differs from the government-wide modified cash column and was not used for balance_sheet. Detail left empty: the only schedule (p8 Budgetary Comparison - All Funds) mixes governmental, utilities and nursing home (7,652,819 nursing home charges not in these statements) in single lines, so fund types cannot be separated; the statement lines already carry the actuals. Transfer cross-check done: governmental net transfer ties to utilities outflow. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
